208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (One of the biggest advantages is cost savings. If you sell your current home and move to a smaller, more affordable space, you may be able to eliminate your mortgage or significantly reduce your monthly expenses. Property taxes, utility bills, and maintenance costs also tend to be lower in a smaller home, giving you more financial flexibility. Whether you want to travel, invest in new hobbies, or simply feel more secure in your finances, rightsizing can help make that possible.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Rightsizing also gives you the opportunity to move closer to loved ones. Maybe you want to be nearer to family, friends, or a community that offers social activities and support. Proximity to healthcare services, grocery stores, and recreational opportunities can also make life easier and more enjoyable. Choosing a home that fits your lifestyle and future needs can help you feel more connected and supported.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Your health and mobility are also important factors to consider. As we age, a home with stairs, heavy upkeep, or difficult-to-reach spaces can become a challenge. Rightsizing allows you to find a home that is safer and more accessible, making daily life easier. Many seniors opt for single-story homes, communities with maintenance services, or locations that offer on-site assistance when needed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
